{
  "valuation_insights": "Costco Wholesale Corporation reported annual total revenue of $303.154 billion for the fiscal year ended August 30, 2026, representing a growth of 10.14% over the prior year [C:revenue_current], [C:revenue_prior], [C:revenue_growth]. Operating income for the year was $11.685 billion, yielding an operating margin of 3.85% [C:operating_income_current], [C:operating_margin]. Net income attributable to the company was $9.226 billion for the fiscal year [C:net_income_current]. The company’s GAAP diluted earnings per share (EPS) were $20.76 [C:diluted_eps_current]. Return on average equity stood at 28.40%, calculated using average shareholders' equity [C:return_on_average_equity]. Costco’s debt to equity ratio, including the current portion of debt, was 0.172 [C:debt_to_equity]. The free cash flow for the fiscal year was $9.382 billion, derived from net cash provided by operations minus capital expenditures [C:free_cash_flow].\n\nFor the latest reported quarter, net sales increased 11.2% to $93.9 billion from $84.4 billion in the same quarter last year [C:quarterly_sales_current], [C:quarterly_sales_prior], [C:quarterly_sales_growth]. Latest quarter GAAP diluted EPS was $6.75 [C:latest_quarter_eps]. However, total quarterly revenue is Not established as the release distinguishes net sales and total revenue, and a tagged total revenue figure for the quarter is not available.\n\nOperating margins of peers on a consistent total revenue basis show Walmart Inc. at 4.18% [C:peer_wmt_operating_margin], Target Corp. at 4.88% [C:peer_tgt_operating_margin], and BJ's Wholesale Club Holdings, Inc. at 3.81% [C:peer_bj_operating_margin]. Costco’s operating margin is slightly lower than Walmart and Target but higher than BJ's.\n\nWith a closing stock price of $904.7 on September 23, 2026, the price-to-earnings (P/E) ratio based on annual GAAP diluted EPS is 43.58 [C:price_to_earnings].\n\n[Caution: The annual revenue is reported using the contract-sales tag; it should be verified to confirm it includes all total revenue components, not just net sales.]",
